{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvyKWe2tUC1LkDQMPvtW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Cwyj5eRDgkGaXadUYdeZfF","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/paper; sed -n 94,97p paper.tex; sed -n 140,143p paper.tex; sed -n 160,170p paper.tex; sed -n 283,292p paper.tex; grep -n -i \"three negative\\|three controls\\|control\" paper.tex | cut -c1-120"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4541,"cache_read_input_tokens":58238,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4541},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ef69e69-c3be-4874-ab3f-3697f6dedd2d","uuid":"92a2415c-4527-4ed8-a7fd-5455cd484542","timestamp":"2026-11-11T10:19:58.561Z","request_id":"req_011CgvyKW3KCTHpjPaVNzeUu"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Cwyj5eRDgkGaXadUYdeZfF","type":"tool_result","content":"The evaluator scores four standard split-conformal baselines on identical data with the same loss, drawn from the score families of Section~\\ref{sec:related}: LAC \\citep{Sadinle2019Least} (threshold on $1-p_y$), APS \\citep{Romano2020Classification} (randomised cumulative-mass score), RAPS \\citep{Angelopoulos2020Uncertainty} (APS with a rank penalty, $\\lambda=0.01$, regularisation start $\\min(5,\\max(1,\\lfloor K/5\\rfloor))$) and class-wise LAC (LAC calibrated per label). Exact implementations are those of the evaluator source, not re-derived from the cited papers. Uncalibrated top-mass, full-set and argmax-only sets are implemented as trivial references. The reported baseline score is that of the best of the four baselines under the aggregated score; the margin is $\\score_{\\mathrm{proc}}-\\score_{\\mathrm{best}}$, and its 95\\% interval is the 2.5--97.5 percentile of 2000 bootstrap resamples of the per-seed paired differences within each case, averaged with equal weight over cases. The interval therefore reflects seed-to-seed variation inside the evaluated cases and not variation across case designs.\n\nThree negative controls are run on one case and seed: (C1) permuted calibration labels, where sets must inflate (size ratio at least $1.5\\times$ the matched case or at least $0.9$); (C2) shuffled test labels, where coverage must not exceed chance by more than a $3\\sigma$ tolerance and must be well below matched coverage or sets near full; (C3) uniform probability inputs, where coverage must be near target and mean set size at least $(1-\\alpha)K-1$. A run is valid only if no episode fails, all controls pass, calibration and test data are content-hash disjoint (and, for the final plane, disjoint from the search data), and exchangeable cases do not under-cover by more than a $3\\sigma$ finite-sample tolerance.\n% @evidence[[sourc