{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvyKmHqfBaAu5dsbZ1Ub","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Lv2sYMK9zRXSpSotfWsjZA","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/paper; python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('paper.tex').read()\ndef rep(a,b,cnt=1):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==cnt,(a,s.count(a))\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"Variants that address one of these questions typically do so at the cost of another \\\\citep{Gibbs2023ConformalPW,Ding2023ClassConditionalCP,Kiyani2024LengthOI}, so comparisons that report only average coverage and average set size can hide the trade-off.\",\n\"Our motivation is that a method tuned for one of these questions may do worse on another, so comparisons that report only average coverage and average set size can hide such differences; recent work on conditional coverage and set efficiency \\\\citep{Gibbs2023ConformalPW,Ding2023ClassConditionalCP,Kiyani2024LengthOI} makes the individual questions concrete, but we do not attribute a general trade-off finding to it.\")\nrep(\"adds three negative controls whose expected behaviour is fixed before scoring\",\"adds negative controls whose expected behaviour is fixed before scoring\")\nrep(\"checked by three negative controls. Scope\",\"checked by negative controls. Scope\")\nrep(\"Conditional conformal prediction has long been studied as a way to reduce bias in label-dependent coverage \\\\citep{Löfström2015BiasRT}, and recent work addresses class-wise coverage when classes are many, long-tailed or have few calibration examples \\\\citep{Ding2023ClassConditionalCP,Ding2025ConformalPF,Shi2024ConformalPF}.\",\n\"Conditional conformal prediction has been proposed for bias reduction \\\\citep{Löfström2015BiasRT}, and recent work addresses class-conditional coverage with many classes \\\\citep{Ding2023ClassConditionalCP}, conformal prediction for long-tailed classification \\\\citep{Ding2025ConformalPF}, and a further class-wise conformal approach \\\\citep{Shi2024ConformalPF}.\")\nrep(\"Three negative controls are run on one case and seed:\",\"In the search-plane evaluator source, three negative controls are defined, each run on one case and seed:\")\nrep(\"A run is valid only if no episode fails, all controls pass,\",\"The number and placement of controls on the final plane are not retained; the sealed record retains only that the controls-passed fraction was 1.0. A run is valid only if no episode fails, all controls pass,\")\nrep(\"No episode failed and all three negative controls passed,\",\"No episode failed and all negative controls passed (controls-passed fraction 1.0; the number of final-plane controls is not retained),\")\nrep(\"Negative controls passed & 3 of 3 (fraction 1.0) \\\\\\\\\",\"Negative controls passed (fraction; count not retained) & 1.0 \\\\\\\\\")\nrep(\"The development score was used to select the configuration, so development numbers are optimistic selection-biased proxies; the sealed evaluation was run once on disjoint data.\",\n\"The development score was used to choose the configuration, so development numbers may be optimistic; this was not measured, and the cause of the drop from the development to the sealed score is not isolated by the retained artifacts. The sealed evaluation was run once on disjoint data.\")\nrep(\"with no failed episodes and all three negative controls passed. The same\",\"with no failed episodes and all negative controls passed. The same\")\nrep(\"A control episode is discarded as vacuous if fewer than half of the permuted labels changed.\",\"In the evaluator, a control episode whose permutation changes fewer than half of the labels is counted as a failed control (\\\\texttt{vacuous\\\\_control}), which invalidates the run.\")\nrep(\"(duration in seconds includes control episodes)\",\"(duration in seconds; what the durations cover is not recorded)\")\nopen('paper.tex','w').write(s)\nE\ngrep -n -i \"three negative\\|3 of 3\\|three controls\\|selection-bias\" paper.tex; sed -n 100,104p validation_feedback.md >/dev/null; grep -n \"Ding2025\\|Shi2024\" references.bib | head; grep -n -A4 \"Ding2025ConformalPF\\|Shi2024ConformalPF\" references.bib | grep -i title"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2415,"cache_read_input_tokens":62779,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2415},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ef69e69-c3be-4874-ab3f-3697f6dedd2d","uuid":"8026dc77-5d3b-4e63-ad5a-76c637f44bc8","timestamp":"2026-11-11T10:20:08.653Z","request_id":"req_011CgvyKki7D1kJJKwQpj6i8"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Lv2sYMK9zRXSpSotfWsjZA","type":"tool_result","content":"36:Softmax outputs are compositions: non-negative vectors summing to one. Conformal prediction turns them into label sets with a finite-sample marginal coverage guarantee, but marginal coverage says little about reliability for particular classes, confidence strata, or shifted data. We study a split-conformal procedure that combines Mondrian (class- or confidence-bin-conditional) calibration of the least-ambiguous-set score with a gated, cross-fitted domain-classifier reweighting step that reduces exactly to the unweighted procedure when no shift is detected. We evaluate it under a fixed, evaluator-owned protocol on synthetic softmax families: a composite score combining one-sided marginal under-coverage, worst-slice under-coverage, and set-size ratio, plus three negative controls. On sealed final data (five seeded runs, no failed episodes, all controls passed) the procedure scores 0.8416 against 0.8029 for the best of four standard split-conformal baselines; the paired margin is 0.0387 (bootstrap 95\\% interval 0.0274--0.0499). Residual under-coverage remains on shifted cases (0.0536) and worst slices (0.0675). The result is conditional on the declared synthetic families; baseline identities, per-case results and real-data behaviour are unavailable.\n96:In the search-plane evaluator source, three negative controls are defined, each run on one case and seed: (C1) permuted calibration labels, where sets must inflate (size ratio at least $1.5\\times$ the matched case or at least $0.9$); (C2) shuffled test labels, where coverage must not exceed chance by more than a $3\\sigma$ tolerance and must be well below matched coverage or sets near full; (C3) uniform probability inputs, where coverage must be near target and mean set size at least $(1-\\alpha)K-1$. The number and placement of controls on the final plane are not retained; the sealed record retains only that the controls-passed fraction was 1.0. A run is valid only if no episode fails, all controls pass, calibration and test data are content-hash disjoint (and, for the final plane, disjoint from the search data), and exchangeable cases do not under-cover by more than a $3\\sigma$ finite-sample tolerance.\n132:\\paragraph{Development data.} V1--V3 are scored with seeds 101--103 on the evaluator's development cases (per the declared reset sequence, three seeds on each of four case designs, plus the three controls); all three configurations produced valid runs and none was unscored. The development score of V2 and V3 tie exactly, and V2 is the configuration recorded by the selection manifest.\n100:@Article{Shi2024ConformalPF,\n131:@Article{Ding2025ConformalPF,\n102- booktitle = {Neural Information Processing Systems},\n104- title = {Conformal Prediction for Class-wise Coverage via Augmented Label Rank Calibration},\n133- booktitle = {International Conference on Learning Representations},\n135- title = {Conformal Prediction for Long-Tailed Classification},","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ef69e69-c3be-4874-ab3f-3697f6dedd2d","uuid":"18dbe8af-63d9-4b6e-94a4-0e0446080dc6","timestamp":"2026-11-11T10:20:08.764Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"36:Softmax outputs are compositions: non-negative vectors summing to one. Conformal prediction turns them into label sets with a finite-sample marginal coverage guarantee, but marginal coverage says little about reliability for particular classes, confidence strata, or shifted data. We study a split-conformal procedure that combines Mondrian (class- or confidence-bin-conditional) calibration of the least-ambiguous-set score with a gated, cross-fitted domain-classifier reweighting step that reduces exactly to the unweighted procedure when no shift is detected. We evaluate it under a fixed, evaluator-owned protocol on synthetic softmax families: a composite score combining one-sided marginal under-coverage, worst-slice under-coverage, and set-size ratio, plus three negative controls. On sealed final data (five seeded runs, no failed episodes, all controls passed) the procedure scores 0.8416 against 0.8029 for the best of four standard split-conformal baselines; the paired margin is 0.0387 (bootstrap 95\\% interval 0.0274--0.0499). Residual under-coverage remains on shifted cases (0.0536) and worst slices (0.0675). The result is conditional on the declared synthetic families; baseline identities, per-case results and real-data behaviour are unavailable.\n96:In the search-plane evaluator source, three negative controls are defined, each run on one case and seed: (C1) permuted calibration labels, where sets must inflate (size ratio at least $1.5\\times$ the matched case or at least $0.9$); (C2) shuffled test labels, where coverage must not exceed chance by more than a $3\\sigma$ tolerance and must be well below matched coverage or sets near full; (C3) uniform probability inputs, where coverage must be near target and mean set size at least $(1-\\alpha)K-1$. The number and placement of controls on the final plane are not retained; the sealed record retains only that the controls-passed fraction was 1.0. A run is valid only if no episode fails, all controls pass, calibration and test data are content-hash disjoint (and, for the final plane, disjoint from the search data), and exchangeable cases do not under-cover by more than a $3\\sigma$ finite-sample tolerance.\n132:\\paragraph{Development data.} V1--V3 are scored with seeds 101--103 on the evaluator's development cases (per the declared reset sequence, three seeds on each of four case designs, plus the three controls); all three configurations produced valid runs and none was unscored. The development score of V2 and V3 tie exactly, and V2 is the configuration recorded by the selection manifest.\n100:@Article{Shi2024ConformalPF,\n131:@Article{Ding2025ConformalPF,\n102- booktitle = {Neural Information Processing Systems},\n104- title = {Conformal Prediction for Class-wise Coverage via Augmented Label Rank Calibration},\n133- booktitle = {International Conference on Learning Representations},\n135- title = {Conformal Prediction for Long-Tailed Classification},","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
