{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvyQH18DdmMV7LFTpqun","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BuxSQQBMk8qtUq2PH4GNJZ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/paper; python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('paper.tex').read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==1,a\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"Our motivation is that a method tuned for one of these questions may do worse on another, so comparisons that report only average coverage and average set size can hide such differences; recent work on conditional coverage and set efficiency \\\\citep{Gibbs2023ConformalPW,Ding2023ClassConditionalCP,Kiyani2024LengthOI} makes the individual questions concrete, but we do not attribute a general trade-off finding to it.\",\n\"Our motivation is that a method tuned for one question may do worse on another, so reporting only average coverage and set size can hide such differences; conditional-coverage and efficiency work \\\\citep{Gibbs2023ConformalPW,Ding2023ClassConditionalCP,Kiyani2024LengthOI} makes the individual questions concrete.\")\nrep(\"The number and placement of controls on the final plane are not retained; the sealed record retains only that the controls-passed fraction was 1.0.\",\"The number of final-plane controls is not retained; only a controls-passed fraction of 1.0 is.\")\nrep(\" (controls-passed fraction 1.0; the number of final-plane controls is not retained)\",\" (fraction 1.0; count not retained)\")\nrep(\"; this was not measured, and the cause of the drop from the development to the sealed score is not isolated by the retained artifacts. The sealed evaluation was run once on disjoint data.\",\"; this was not measured, and the cause of the development-to-sealed drop is not isolated. The sealed evaluation was run once on disjoint data.\")\nopen('paper.tex','w').write(s)\nE\nsed -n 205,222p paper.tex | cut -c1-400"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1203,"cache_read_input_tokens":77407,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1203},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ef69e69-c3be-4874-ab3f-3697f6dedd2d","uuid":"e14b9b40-f08e-4b9a-a08e-023c04e0de83","timestamp":"2026-11-11T10:21:05.635Z","request_id":"req_011CgvyQGA2NanJkYPToJ3JM"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BuxSQQBMk8qtUq2PH4GNJZ","type":"tool_result","content":"\\paragraph{What it does not support.}\n(i) \\emph{Real data.} No real-data run exists; behaviour on classifier outputs from natural datasets is untested.\n(ii) \\emph{Baseline identity.} Only the best baseline score is retained; we cannot say which baseline it is or how the others compare.\n(iii) \\emph{Cases and families.} Per-case and per-family results, $\\alpha$ and sample sizes of the sealed cases are unknown; the bootstrap interval does not cover variation across case designs.\n(iv) \\emph{Mechanism.} The comparison among V1--V3 is a design comparison on three seeds and does not isolate the contribution of any single component of the weighting step; V3 provides no information on quantile regression.\n(v) \\emph{Validity versus statistics.} The residual shift and slice gaps are reported as measured; the diagnostics needed to separate estimation error in the density ratio, small-sample noise and violated assumptions are not available, and candidate-side diagnostics are unverified.\n(vi) \\emph{Range.} The tested range is limited by the evaluator ($K\\le100$, $n_{\\mathrm{cal}}\\le2000$); nothing is claimed about larger $K$, very small calibration sets, or simplex-valued regression targets.\n(vii) \\emph{Metric.} One-sided gap metrics do not penalise over-coverage except through set size, and the Mondrian guarantee is conditional on label or confidence bin, not on arbitrary slices, so slice gaps in other partitions are not controlled by theory.\n\n\\paragraph{Evidence inventory.} Table~\\ref{tab:inventory} (Supplementary Information) separates available from unknown quantities, so gaps are not mistaken for null results.\n\n\\paragraph{Threats to validity.}\nThe synthetic generator is one parametric family (Gaussian logits with a true-class signal, heteroscedastic signal strength, a prior tilt and temperature), and the predictor's calibration is not varied independently; real softmax outputs may behave differently. For $K\\le10$ the evaluator's slices are classes, which are exactly the Mondrian groups of the studied procedure, so part of its advantage \n\n\\paragraph{What would change the conclusion.} The positive margin would be weakened if per-baseline results showed that the best baseline wins on the slice or size axis and loses only on a few shifted cases, or if the sealed cases were mostly shifted. It would be strengthened by per-case margins whose intervals all exclude zero, by gate logs showing the gate closed on exchangeable cases, and by re\n\n\\paragraph{Practical reading.} For users, the results suggest evaluating conformal sets on compositional outputs with at least a marginal, a slice-level and a size criterion, and with controls that expose vacuous behaviour; reporting only average coverage and size would not have revealed the residual shift and slice gaps seen here. A stronger study built on the same protocol would additionally rep","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ef69e69-c3be-4874-ab3f-3697f6dedd2d","uuid":"1189c047-9307-4c00-91ed-cba10b9b06c2","timestamp":"2026-11-11T10:21:05.709Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"\\paragraph{What it does not support.}\n(i) \\emph{Real data.} No real-data run exists; behaviour on classifier outputs from natural datasets is untested.\n(ii) \\emph{Baseline identity.} Only the best baseline score is retained; we cannot say which baseline it is or how the others compare.\n(iii) \\emph{Cases and families.} Per-case and per-family results, $\\alpha$ and sample sizes of the sealed cases are unknown; the bootstrap interval does not cover variation across case designs.\n(iv) \\emph{Mechanism.} The comparison among V1--V3 is a design comparison on three seeds and does not isolate the contribution of any single component of the weighting step; V3 provides no information on quantile regression.\n(v) \\emph{Validity versus statistics