{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L1oNsvLYYstF8Ury7acwVg","type":"tool_result","content":"\\paragraph{Practical reading.} For users, the results suggest evaluating conformal sets on compositional outputs with at least a marginal, a slice-level and a size criterion, and with controls that expose vacuous behaviour; reporting only average coverage and size would not have revealed the residual shift and slice gaps seen here. A stronger study built on the same protocol would additionally report per-baseline and per-case scores, a within-case ablation that separates the Mondrian grouping, the gate and the weighting, activation logs for the gate, and at least one evaluation on classifier outputs from a natural dataset. We also recommend reporting the three components separately for every method (Figure~\\ref{fig:decomp}).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ef69e69-c3be-4874-ab3f-3697f6dedd2d","uuid":"7c848b05-4d18-4753-821b-1d5a032c1fb7","timestamp":"2026-11-11T10:21:08.640Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"\\paragraph{Practical reading.} For users, the results suggest evaluating conformal sets on compositional outputs with at least a marginal, a slice-level and a size criterion, and with controls that expose vacuous behaviour; reporting only average coverage and size would not have revealed the residual shift and slice gaps seen here. A stronger study built on the same protocol would additionally report per-baseline and per-case scores, a within-case ablation that separates the Mondrian grouping, the gate and the weighting, activation logs for the gate, and at least one evaluation on classifier outputs from a natural dataset. We also recommend reporting the three components separately for every method (Figure~\\ref{fig:decomp}).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
